  "goodToKnow": "Die Demontage is dismantling: die Demontage einer Anlage. After 1945, the Allies, especially the Soviet Union in its zone, dismantled German factories as reparations, the Demontagen. Figuratively, die Demontage of a person means systematically destroying their reputation: politische Demontage. Demontieren means to dismantle; the opposite is die Montage (assembly). The g is soft as in French. Plural: die Demontagen."
